{"kind":"request","text":"R14 partial: the usage report script (child of R14 bb763efa).\n\nFiled at the builder's request 6963d597 so the landing closes this\nchild and not R14, which still owes individual routes, native platform\nversions and features beyond the current telemetry (gaps recorded in\n244115c5).\n\nScope, as accepted in c0832d1f:\n- scripts/usage-report.mjs with focused Node fixtures, a schema for\n  the mapping file and a short docs page.\n- One bounded 30-day aggregate Analytics query. The token comes only\n  from bounded stdin, never from an argument, a file or the\n  environment, and never appears in output.\n- The Worker-to-deployment mapping is an operator-supplied JSON file\n  outside the repository, passed by path; the script refuses a Worker\n  it cannot map and says so in the report. The repository holds the\n  schema and a sample fixture only.\n- The report gives each configured route or binding one of three\n  statuses, observed, zero-observed or unobservable, against the\n  current static configuration inventory, and states the coverage,\n  sampling and loss limits. It says \"no observed use\" where coverage\n  cannot prove absence, never \"never used\".\n- Witnesses: recorded TEST emissions, and separately labelled scripted\n  responses; no invented hosted SQL evidence; no live query in the\n  gate; no Worker setting; no builder deployment.\n\nConditions: one head over Main; ordinary gate at the exact head; PD-2\nnote and manifest; named witnesses with paired controls for token\nnon-disclosure, the unmappable Worker refusal, truncation and the\nstatus wording; one checker review at the exact head before landing.\nOrder: after R11 item 6 (ee18ccc1) and the BR-4 completion (f76f93d3);\narchive work under 0f0eeab7 preempts it. The planner runs the script\nfirst with its own token and files the first report under R14.","body":{"conditions":"One head over Main: ordinary gate at the exact head, PD-2 note and manifest, paired-control witnesses 